{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>And the children struggled.</b> This verse cries out, 'Interpret me!' — for Scripture left unexplained what this רְצִיצָה is, and wrote, ״If so, why am I thus?״ Our Sages interpreted it as a term of running: when she would pass by the entrances to the Torah academies of Shem and Eber, Jacob would run and struggle to come out; when she would pass by the entrance to idol worship, Esau would struggle to come out. Another interpretation: they struggled with one another and quarreled over the inheritance of the two worlds." "<b>And she said, If so.</b> Great is the distress of pregnancy." "<b>Why am I thus.</b> She longs and prays regarding the pregnancy:" "<b>And she went to inquire.</b> To the academy of Shem:" "<b>To inquire of YHWH.</b> That he would tell her what would be in her end:"], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:00:28.046700523Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}